motion-control plugin factory. params (all optional):
plant: "dynamic" | "ideal";  env: "core-default" | "legacy" | {atmos:{..}, wind:{..}};
axes: {pan:{J,wn_hz,zeta,tau_max,w_max_deg_s,b}, tilt:{..}};  payload: {...};  clock: "wall" | "external";
units_per_deg / zero_native (native quantisation, as native_simulator).

Screen one formulation; every number returned is a cite value record.

formulation keys:
  resin        -- resins.json id
  components   -- [{"id", "wt"} ...] additive loadings in wt%
  fillers      -- [{"id", "wt", "length_mm", "ifss_mpa"} ...]
  feedstock    -- {moisture_ppm, cooh_mmol_kg, iv_dl_g, water_reacted_fraction,
                   ipa_mol_pct, deg_mol_pct, ...}
  process      -- {melt_temp_c, residence_s, mold_temp_c, vent_mbar, epoxy_conversion}
  targets      -- {tensile_mpa, hdt_c, clarity, food_contact, process}
  composite    -- optional {orientation_factor, matrix_stress_mpa} (defaults 0.4, 55)

Normalise the loads input into (point_loads, point_moms, dist).

point_loads: [(P, a)] with P downward positive; point_moms: [(M, a)] with M CCW positive;
dist: [(wa, wb, a, b)] trapezoidal loads (wa at a, wb at b) downward positive, wa == wb for a UDL.

Present/future/annual worth and discounted payback of a cash-flow series at rate i.

Cash flows are [CF0, CF1, ...] with CF0 at t = 0 (negative for an outlay). NPV = Σ CF_t/(1+i)^t;
future worth is compounded to the end of the last period; annual worth spreads NPV uniformly;
discounted payback is the first time the cumulative discounted flow reaches zero (linearly
interpolated within the crossing period).

Injection-molding cooling time: first Fourier term of a slab cooled from both faces.

profile='mean' uses the mean (thickness-averaged) temperature coefficient 8/π²;
profile='centreline' uses the mid-plane coefficient 4/π.

Coupler angle theta3 (rad) for a four-bar at crank angle th2.

``br`` selects the assembly: +1 gives theta4 = phi + beta (crossed) and -1 gives phi - beta (open);
theta3 is the coupler angle of the same branch.
